# Audience

People browsing `reports/**` and running `ttnn-accuracy measure`, `compare`, `check`,
`perf`, `history`. Not kernel-generating models, not RL reward.

- Cite arch/dtype/op/variant and the tt-metal commit.
- Never average across architectures or dtypes. Never extrapolate an unmeasured cell.
- A sampled `max_ulp` is a lower bound. `refine` is how to tighten one.
- Never compare a timing across hosts.
- Never penalise `faithful` (WH/BH `NearestAway` vs torch even).
- `compare`: `rounded_frac` higher is better; do not subtract `max_ulp` when only the
  candidate has `rounded_frac` (wider-reference definition change).
- `ask.md` is generated from `contract.md`. Regenerate it; do not hand-edit.
